<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  TEMPLATE. Do not install this file directly — run schedule/install.sh, which
  substitutes __HOME__ and __REPO__ and loads the result. launchd does not expand
  ~ or $HOME inside a plist, so every path here has to be absolute, which is why
  a template plus a renderer beats a checked-in copy of somebody's home dir.

  Weekly harvest of the public-sector open source catalogues, followed by the
  liveness monitor, a regenerated page, and the publish step.
  (run.sh documents the step ordering and why it is what it is.)

  WEEKLY, not daily, deliberately. These catalogues move slowly — one observed
  change in a day was code.europa.eu going 9 -> 12 entries. A full run costs
  ~25 min of network I/O against other people's public infrastructure, so daily
  would be rude for no added signal. The liveness delta is the part worth
  watching, and dead repos do not appear faster than weekly either.

  PATH is set explicitly because launchd jobs get a minimal environment:
    /opt/homebrew/bin              -> gh, used by liveness.py for a GitHub token
                                      (5000 req/hr GraphQL instead of anonymous
                                      HEAD, which is what caused a 27% 429 rate)
    .../Python.framework/3.12/bin  -> a python3 that actually has pyyaml+certifi
    __HOME__/.npm-global/bin       -> vercel, for the final publish step
    /usr/local/bin                 -> node. The vercel CLI's shebang is
                                      `#!/usr/bin/env node`, so without this the
                                      publish step dies with "env: node: No such
                                      file or directory" — which looks like an
                                      auth failure and is not. Prefer a versionless
                                      node path: an nvm one carries a version
                                      number and moves on every upgrade.
  If `gh` is missing, liveness degrades to HEAD rather than failing.
  run.sh probes for its own python3 regardless, so a wrong Framework path here
  costs nothing — it is listed for speed, not correctness.

  PUBLISHING: with node on PATH, the Vercel CLI's stored login works from a
  launchd job (verify with `env -i PATH=<this PATH> HOME=$HOME vercel whoami`).
  A token is still preferable, since a stored login can be revoked and would then
  fail every week: run.sh reads VERCEL_TOKEN, then ~/.config/govoss/vercel-token
  (chmod 600), then falls back to the stored login. The FILE is the preferred
  route, which is why no token appears below — LaunchAgent plists are
  world-readable and get swept into backups, and rotating a token in a file needs
  no launchctl reload. Create tokens at https://vercel.com/account/tokens.

  NL_API_KEY is intentionally absent — the Dutch OSS register needs a key that
  has not been requested, so harvest.py skips that source and says so. Add it as
  an EnvironmentVariables entry once you have one. (The Dutch *code platform* at
  code.overheid.nl needs no key and is harvested; only the register is gated.)

  Run now: launchctl kickstart -k gui/$UID/org.antigravity.govoss-harvest
  Status:  launchctl print gui/$UID/org.antigravity.govoss-harvest | head -20
  Unload:  launchctl bootout gui/$UID/org.antigravity.govoss-harvest
  Log:     __HOME__/Library/Logs/govoss-harvest.log  (stdout AND stderr, appended)
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>org.antigravity.govoss-harvest</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/bash</string>
    <string>__REPO__/run.sh</string>
  </array>

  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>__REPO__</string>

  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/Library/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.12/bin:__HOME__/.npm-global/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
    <key>HOME</key>
    <string>__HOME__</string>
  </dict>

  <!-- Mondays at 07:00 local -->
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <dict>
    <key>Weekday</key><integer>1</integer>
    <key>Hour</key><integer>7</integer>
    <key>Minute</key><integer>0</integer>
  </dict>

  <!--
    If the Mac is asleep or off at 07:00, launchd runs the job once soon after
    wake rather than skipping the week — that is StartCalendarInterval's own
    behaviour for missed occurrences, so no extra key is needed. (An earlier
    revision of this file claimed StartOnMount did that; it does not — that key
    is about filesystem mounts and was removed.)
  -->
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>__HOME__/Library/Logs/govoss-harvest.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>__HOME__/Library/Logs/govoss-harvest.log</string>

  <key>ProcessType</key>
  <string>Background</string>

  <key>LowPriorityIO</key>
  <true/>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <false/>
</dict>
</plist>
